      "body": "pore-facing hydroxyl groups from OH-IPA → uptake"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] pre-functionalize the MAC-4 linker with hydroxyl groups by replacing IPA with 5-hydroxyisophthalic acid to form MAC-4-OH → CO2 uptake is significantly enhanced in MAC-4-OH relative to MAC-4, despite lower surface area"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] construct MOFs using metal-cluster secondary building units as mononodes, including combined trinuclear-triangular and paddle-wheel SBUs → provides an efficient and feasible route to synthesize various porous and functionalized MOFs"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "MAC-4-OH vs MAC-4: winner=subject_a on CO2_initial_uptake_rate"
    }
